{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "document_id": "ch-preps-addinguser",
  "title": "Adding the LFS User",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When logged in as user"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", making a single mistake can damage or destroy a system. Therefore, the packages in the next two chapters are built as an unprivileged user. You could use your own user name, but to make it easier to set up a clean working environment, we will create a new user called"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "as a member of a new group (also named"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ") and run commands as"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "during the installation process. As"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", issue the following commands to add the new user:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "system_operation_command",
      "index": 0,
      "source_index": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "definition_list",
      "entries": [
        {
          "term": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "-s /bin/bash"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This makes"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "bash"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the default shell for user"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "lfs"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "-g lfs"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This option adds user"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "lfs"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "to group"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "lfs"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "-m"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This creates a home directory for"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "lfs"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "-k /dev/null"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This parameter prevents possible copying of files from a skeleton directory (the default is"
                },
                {
                  "type": "code",
                  "text": "/etc/skel"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ") by changing the input location to the special null device."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "lfs"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This is the name of the new user."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "title": "This is what the command line options mean:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If you want to log in as"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "or switch to"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "from a non-"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "user (as opposed to switching to user"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "when logged in as"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", which does not require the"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "user to have a password), you need to set a password for"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Issue the following command as the"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "user to set the password:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "system_operation_command",
      "index": 1,
      "source_index": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Grant"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "full access to all the directories under"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "$LFS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "by making"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "the owner:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "system_operation_command",
      "index": 2,
      "source_index": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "kind": "note",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In some host systems, the following"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "su"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "command does not complete properly and suspends the login for the"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "lfs"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "user to the background. If the prompt \"lfs:~$\" does not appear immediately, entering the"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "fg"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "command will fix the issue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next, start a shell running as user"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". This can be done by logging in as"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "lfs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "on a virtual console, or with the following substitute/switch user command:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "system_operation_command",
      "index": 3,
      "source_index": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "instructs"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "su"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "to start a login shell as opposed to a non-login shell. The difference between these two types of shells is described in detail in"
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://man.archlinux.org/man/bash.1",
          "label": "bash(1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "and"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "info bash"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
